.Dd October 9, 2026
.Dt BSDTIME 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BSDTime
.Nd system.Time capability provider
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the
.Dq system.Time
capability provider: the trusted broker for setting the system wall clock.
A holder of a system.Time channel reads
.Dv CLOCK_REALTIME
or, when policy permits, steps it with
.Xr clock_settime 2
or slews it with
.Xr adjtime 2 ,
instead of calling those privileged syscalls directly.
Clients use
.Xr libtimecmp 3 .
.Pp
.Nm
is
.Em born in capability mode :
switchboard execs it already inside the Capsicum cage.
Moving the clock needs
.Dv PRIV_SETTIMEOFDAY ,
which capability mode strips, so
.Nm
holds a
.Dq system
gate token delivered by switchboard and steps the clock
.Em through
that token in kernel context; the raw
.Xr settimeofday 2
stays refused inside the cage, so the sandbox is never loosened.
It is launched by
.Xr switchboard 8
as the
.Pa /Capabilities/System/Time.cap
bundle and never started by hand.
The gate token remains in one process, which multiplexes client channels with
.Xr kqueue 2 .
The security boundary is the Capsicum sandbox plus the per-label policy.
.Sh RESOURCE LIMITS
The provider admits at most 32 sessions and eight sessions per trusted client
label.
Excess connections are closed while existing sessions continue.
Idle sessions expire after 30 seconds.
Each ready peer receives one bounded dispatch batch, at most 64 messages,
with the starting peer rotating between iterations.
A session may queue at most 16 replies and 4096 bytes, with no descriptors.
A nonreading peer that exhausts its reply queue is closed.
Quiescing closes all sessions before acknowledging completion.
.Sh PROTOCOL
The source implementation uses the generated C bindings for
.Li bsd.time.v1
from
.Pa /usr/share/fidl/timecmp.fidl .
Clients first call GetProtocolInfo and verify wire version 1 before Get, Set,
or Adjust.
Legacy messages, unknown methods, malformed messages, and unexpected descriptors
close the session.
Application errors remain distinct from transport errors.
.Pp
Set uses signed seconds and a nonnegative nanosecond fraction.
Adjust uses signed seconds and signed microseconds, preserving negative deltas.
Policy checks precede application range checks and gate calls.
.Ss Migration status
The FIDL provider/client migration is implemented in the source tree and has
native host tests; activation, real-gate VM tests, and rollback validation
remain required.
The bundle advances to version 2.0.0, sequence 2.
Deploy or roll back the provider and its matching libtimecmp together;
restart provider and consumers to avoid mixed in-memory wire implementations.
Do not replay clock writes after an ambiguous transport failure.
.Sh POLICY
Reading the clock is unprivileged and allowed to every holder.
Stepping and slewing are
.Em default-deny :
a label may move the clock only if
.Pa Config/time.conf
grants it.
The file is UCL:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
default { set = false; }
clients {
	"org.5bsd.ntp" { set = true; }
}
.Ed
.Pp
A label matches by exact string.
An unlisted label falls back to
.Va default .
A missing or malformed
.Pa time.conf
is fail-soft: the built-in default-deny stands.
Stepping the clock is dangerous \(em a backward step invalidates TLS
certificate validity windows, audit ordering, and Kerberos tickets \(em so
grant
.Va set
only to a trusted time source.
.Sh TESTS
The
.Li 5BSD-bsdtime-tests
package installs provider and policy tests under
.Pa /usr/tests/usr.sbin/BSDTime .
The provider tests use real channels with simulated clock writes.
The separate real-gate test requires explicit
.Li vm_clock_test=true
configuration in a disposable VM; it is disabled by default.
The auxiliary
.Pa /usr/tests/usr.sbin/BSDTime/resource_soak
program takes an explicit duration in seconds (1 through 86400).
It repeatedly reconnects eight C clients and four idle peers in capability
mode, checking policy results, descriptor cleanup, and allocation growth.
Clock writes and logging are simulated.
Runs shorter than 30 seconds are reported as smoke checks.
This program is not included in ordinary Kyua runs.
Split test debugging symbols are in
.Li 5BSD-bsdtime-tests-dbg .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /Capabilities/System/Time.cap/Units/bsdtime.unit/Config/time.conf
per-label clock-write policy
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr adjtime 2 ,
.Xr clock_settime 2 ,
.Xr libtimecmp 3 ,
.Xr switchboard 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
